  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 115 AM MDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nFlow aloft becomes more westerly through the day Friday, as another\nembedded wave translates across the Intermountain West. The drier air\ncontinues to across the region, with little to no convection expected\nacross the area on Friday. The dry air and downslope flow will bring\nspotty critical fire weather conditions to areas along the ContDvd \ninto the interior valleys and the portions of the I-25 Corridor\non Friday. Temperatures warm back above seasonal levels on Friday,\nwith highs mainly in the 90s across the plains, and int the 60s, 70s\nand 80s across the higher terrain.  \n\nFor Saturday, Sunday and Monday, models continue to indicate ebbs and \nflows of available moisture and forcing as occasional waves translate \nthrough the moderate to strong westerly flow aloft across the Northern \nTier. This will bring chances of precipitation and cooler temperatures \nwith fronts across the Plains on Saturday and again on Monday. \n\nThere looks to be another influx of subtropical moisture across the Desert \nSW and back into Colorado into the middle of next week, bringing better\nchances of precipitation areawide, and likely cooler temperatures.",
